# <%= current_page.data.title %>

Replace this page with your own home page. It is the first thing a reader sees and
the entry point for the sidebar navigation.

A good home page answers three questions in the first screenful: what this site
covers, who it is for, and where to go next.

## Getting started

If you have just created this repository from the template, work through
[SETUP.md](https://github.com/hmcts/docs-as-code-template/blob/main/SETUP.md)
before writing content — a few settings have to be changed by hand.

## Sections

Group related pages into sections. Each section is a folder under `source/` with
an `index.html.md.erb` that lists its pages, which is what the sidebar renders.

| Section | Contents |
|---|---|
| [Example Section](example-section/index.html) | A worked example — one section index and one page |

## Adding a page

Ask your coding agent to add a page rather than copying files by hand:

```
/docs-site add a page about how our deployment pipeline works
```

The skill interviews you, creates the file from `.github/page-template.md`
with the correct frontmatter, updates the section index, and checks the result.
